{#- Rootful Podman with Quadlet units. Containers come from consuming
   formulas via podman/macros.jinja (`container`, `network`); this file only
   holds the defaults the macro fills in.

   subid: the range rootful `--userns=auto` carves per-container user
   namespaces from. Podman 5.4.2 (Debian trixie) looks up the name
   `containers` in /etc/subuid and /etc/subgid — the `storage` in the
   commented storage.conf default is stale (checked on homepage,
   2026-11-12). No account of that name is needed. Kept clear of the
   login accounts' ranges (100000+), which useradd hands out.

   firewall_driver: netavark keeps its rules in its own nft table
   (inet netavark). Pinned so podman.migrate's cleanup of Docker's
   leftover iptables tables can never hit netavark's rules.

   docker_units: stopped and disabled by podman.migrate on a host that
   still has Docker (one runtime per VM). formulas/docker stays in the
   repo, unused; the packages and /var/lib/docker stay on the VM until
   removed by hand (README "Migration from Docker").

   container: defaults for every container — hardening on (NoNewPrivileges,
   all capabilities dropped, read-only root with tmpfs for /tmp, /run,
   /var/tmp), own user namespace from the subid range. A formula opts out
   per container (cap_add, read_only: False, …) — see README "Container
   spec" for every key.
   stop_timeout: seconds podman waits after SIGTERM before SIGKILL, also on
   a backup's `systemctl stop` (formulas/backup) — SQLite apps get time to
   close their DB.
   timeout_start_sec: covers an image pull at boot if the image is gone;
   Salt pulls before it starts a unit, so a normal start is seconds. #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'pkgs': ['podman', 'crun', 'netavark', 'aardvark-dns', 'catatonit'],
    'bin': '/usr/bin/podman',
    'quadlet_dir': '/etc/containers/systemd',
    'conf_dropin': '/etc/containers/containers.conf.d/50-salt.conf',
    'log_driver': 'journald',
    'firewall_driver': 'nftables',
    'subid': {
        'name': 'containers',
        'start': 2147483647,
        'size': 2147483648,
        'files': ['/etc/subuid', '/etc/subgid'],
    },
    'docker_units': ['docker.socket', 'docker.service', 'containerd.service'],
    'container': {
        'image': '',
        'tag': '',
        'user': '',
        'userns': 'auto',
        'keep_uids': [],
        'keep_gids': [],
        'no_new_privileges': True,
        'drop_caps': ['ALL'],
        'cap_add': [],
        'read_only': True,
        'privileged': False,
        'ports': [],
        'volumes': [],
        'tmpfs': [],
        'devices': [],
        'group_add': [],
        'env': {},
        'secret_env': {},
        'command': [],
        'network': '',
        'hostname': '',
        'podman_args': [],
        'unit': {},
        'wanted_by': ['multi-user.target'],
        'restart': 'always',
        'stop_timeout': 60,
        'timeout_start_sec': 900,
    },
} %}
{%- set podman = salt['pillar.get']('podman:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
